    "How long the hive spends attacking before it pulls back to regroup, and vice versa, IN SECONDS. The state flips on this timer and drives every alien at once: attacking they hunt the player, regrouping they retreat. Each period is randomised by up to an eighth, so the swarm does not move like clockwork.\n32000 (about 8.9 hours, the commonest retail value) effectively means 'always attacking'. The engine's own default is 60": "",
    "How long the run takes. Stored as 16.16 seconds, the same unit as the fan's spin-up time. Retail uses 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 3, 5, 7 and 10 seconds": "",
